      {
        "id": "iRc4WOvHCwl4gS8E",
        "title": "Adding Outputs",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>Did you notice the blocks come in three different colors?</p><ul><li>The purple blocks are called “signals.” They bring new signals into the program in the form of numbers.</li><li>The blue blocks are called “operators.” They operate on (do something with) those numbers inside the program.</li></ul><p>Now we can add a yellow block. These are devices. A &quot;live device&quot; makes something happen in real life or in a simulation. A &quot;demo device&quot; just shows a demo in the Dataflow program - it doesn&#x27;t connect to anything outside the program.</p><p>Click the “demo device” to add a tile to your workspace. Use the dropdown menu to change it into a gripper.</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
