      {
        "id": "0co2DJMvj50mCYaY",
        "title": "Extension opportunity: AI Discussion",
        "display": "teacher",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p>If you have time and want to extend, you can have a class discussion around here about AI tools. Some topics you can discuss are:</p><ul><li>What are different things you can ask of AI? What is AI maybe <em>not</em> so good at?</li><li>Who should you ask for what kind of help? (e.g., AI, friends/peers, the teacher) What are other ways to get help? (e.g., reviewing your prior work, thinking, looking at the lesson)</li><li>What are we curious about regarding what Ada might be able to help us with?</li><li>How can we tell whether AI tools are trustworthy in general?</li><li>How are AI tools developed? (e.g., discussion around training sets, text completion -- you may want to note that Ada Ideas was specially trained to align with this curriculum)</li></ul><p>After students have tried Ada Ideas:</p><ul><li>How is Ada Ideas different from or similar to other AI tools they have used?</li><li>What can different AI tools look like or be used for? (The AIdeas chatbot is similar to ChatGPT, but students might not have realized that the sorting tool in the class portfolio is also run by AI. You can also bring up ideas like automatic detection of cancer cells)</li><li>Is Ada Ideas trustworthy? How can we tell? Is Ada Ideas trustworthy about everything or just about some things?</li><li>Do we have any tips for improving Ada Ideas?</li><li>What do we want to pay attention to in future lessons?</li><li>What strategies can we suggest for using AI tools like Ada effectively? (or specifically using Ada effectively in this unit)</li></ul><p>Note: You do not have to have this kind of discussion -- this is only an extension opportunity. An alternative is making an exit ticket question around Ada Ideas.</p><p>Additionally, if you <em>do </em>decide to have a class discussion here, you should just choose one or two main questions to explore.</p>"
          ]
        }
